{"abstract":"Surgical total hip arthroplasty (THA) is associated with high risk of venous thromboembolism (VTE), but the appropriate duration of postoperative anticoagulation remains controversial. “Enhanced Recovery and Abbreviated Length of Anticoagulation for Thromboprophylaxis After Primary Hip Arthroplasty” (ENABLE-Hip) is a multicenter investigator-initiated and academically sponsored randomized double-blind active-control non-inferiority trial. Patients will be mobilized early after surgery, following a standardized enhanced recovery protocol. After an initial open-label prophylactic anticoagulation as per local standard of care until day 2 after surgery, treatment with rivaroxaban (10 mg once daily) will be started on day 3 and continued until day 10. Subsequently, patients will be switched to placebo in the experimental arm, or continue on active drug in the control arm, until a total of 35 days. The primary endpoint is acute symptomatic or fatal VTE within 3 months. A sample size of 2,932 patients will provide ≥ 80% power to reject the null hypothesis that δ ≥ 0.01 (δ = difference between the two arms in symptomatic VTE probability) at a significance level α = 0.05. An interim analysis will be performed after 3-month follow-up of the first 1,760 randomized patients at a significance level α = 0.50, leading to stop for futility if significance is not obtained, or if recalculation yields a sample size of > 3,200 patients. ENABLE-Hip will be the first major randomized trial to test an overall reduction in the duration of post-THA thromboprophylaxis and will inform future guideline recommendations concerning this continuously growing patient population. Trial registration: ClinicalTrials.gov","author_count":29,"contributors":["Drees, Philipp","Schmidtmann, Irene","Herbst, Manuel","Becker, Dorothea","Barco, Stefano","Klok, Frederikus A.","Keller, Karsten","Hobohm, Lukas","Christodoulou, Konstantinos C.","Abele, Christina","Bauersachs, Rupert","Ageno, Walter","Grove, Erik Lerkevang","Kehlet, Henrik","Hufen, Friedhelm","Klonschinski, Thomas","Afghanyar, Yama","Eckhard, Lukas","Martin, Nadine","Fischer, Susanne","Gorbulev, Stanislav","Rath, Dominik","Mavromanoli, Anna C.","Jabbour, Claude","Lang, Irene","Couturaud, Francis","Heiss, Christian","Binder, Harald","Konstantinides, Stavros"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-816710"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Konstantinides, Stavros"],"country":["Austria","France","Germany","Italy","Netherlands","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Centre Hospitalier Universitaire de Brest","ETH Zürich","Justus Liebig University Giessen","Leiden University Medical Center","Markus-Krankenhaus Frankfurt","Medical University of Vienna","Tübingen University Hospital","University Hospital Mannheim","University of Freiburg","University of Padova","Universitätsmedizin Mainz"],"keyword":["Anticoagulation","Randomized Controlled Trial","Thromboprophylaxis","Total hip arthroplasty","Venous thromboembolism"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enhanced recovery and abbreviated length of anticoagulation for thromboprophylaxis after primary hip arthroplasty rationale and design of the enable hip trial","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11239-025-03110-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-816710","identifier":[{"id":"105006823637","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40442449","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12350570","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-d3ae0c85-8a55-4e75-8036-7bc13c613e95"],"keyword":["Anticoagulation","Randomized controlled trial","Thromboprophylaxis","Total hip arthroplasty","Venous thromboembolism"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-60B9D26ED419FC7BC67E2C4FFA909BE8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11239-025-03110-5","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"universitätsmedizin mainz","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universitätsmedizin Mainz","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"eth zürich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"ETH Zürich","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"leiden university medical center","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leiden University Medical Center","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"markus krankenhaus frankfurt","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Markus-Krankenhaus Frankfurt","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"it","key":"university of padova","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Padova","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["National Hospital of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"de","key":"tübingen university hospital","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Tübingen University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"de","key":"university hospital