ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-12d2e3e0-cec2-40e9-a5a7-ea346a07783e","sdu-bd1f99e0-3fa9-4a25-bd3b-5807f85940dc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Psychometric properties and socio-demographic correlates of the Connor-Davidson Resilience Scale in three large population-based cohorts including Danish and Icelandic adults","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.59-822899","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Pediatric patients have an increased risk of radiation-induced malignancies due to their ongoing development and long remaining life span. Thus, optimization of PET protocols is an important task in pediatric nuclear medicine. Long axial field-of-view (LAFOV) PET/CT has shown a significant increase in sensitivity, which provides an ideal opportunity for reduction of injected tracer activity in the pediatric population. In this study we aim to evaluate the clinical performance of a 2-[18F]FDG-tracer reduction from 3 MBq/kg to 1.5 MBq/kg on the Biograph Vision Quadra LAFOV PET/CT. Materials and methods: The first 50 pediatric patients referred for clinical whole-body PET/CT with 1.5 MBq/kg 2-[18F]FDG, were included. A standard pediatric protocol was applied. Five reconstructions were created with various time, filter and iteration settings. Image noise was computed as coefficient-of-variance (COV = SD/mean standardized-uptake-value) calculated from a spherical 20–50 mm (diameter) liver volume-of-interest. Sets of reconstructions were reviewed by one nuclear medicine physicians, who reported image lesions on a pre-defined list of sites. Paired comparison analysis was performed with significance at PB < 0.05 (Bonferroni corrected). Results: All reconstructions, except one, achieved a COVmean (0.08–0.15) equal to or lower than current clinical acceptable values (COVref ≤ 0.15). Image noise significantly improved with increasing acquisition time, lowering iterations (i) from 6i to 4i (both with five subsets) and when applying a 2 mm Gauss filter (PB < 0.001). Significant difference in lesion detection was seen from 150s to 300s and from 150s to 600s (PB = 0.006–0.007). 99% of all lesions rated as malignant could be found on the 150s reconstruction, while 100% was found on the 300s, when compared to the 600s reconstruction. Conclusion: Injected activity and scan time can be reduced to 1.5 MBq/kg 2-[18F]FDG with 5 min acquisition time on LAFOV PET/CT, while maintaining clinical performance in the pediatric population. These results can help limit radiation exposure to patients and personnel as well as shorten total scan time, which can help increase patient comfort, lessen the need for sedation and provide individually tailored scans.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Honoré d’Este, Sabrina","Andersen, Flemming Littrup","Schulze, Christina","Saxtoft, Eunice","Fischer, Barbara Malene","Andersen, Kim Francis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747374"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","King's College London"],"keyword":["LAFOV","Pediatric imaging","Quadra"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"qualipaed a retrospective quality control study evaluating pediatric long axial field of view low dose fdg pet ct","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fnume.2024.1398773","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747374","identifier":[{"id":"85197575046","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11440848","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39355209","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-057995b6-0e50-4ced-a354-03706ca1625e"],"keyword":["LAFOV","Quadra","low-Dose 2-[18F]FDG","pediatric imaging","total-body PET/CT"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-50F9D35DB25B2C1C2EAA24E0012C338A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fnume.2024.1398773","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/398557245/fnume_04_1398773.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Physiology and Nuclear Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"king s college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"King's College London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sabrina","key":"honorédestesabrinapau","last":"Honoré d’Este","name":"Honoré d’Este, Sabrina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Flemming Littrup","key":"andersenflemminglittruppau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Flemming Littrup","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"schulzechristinapau","last":"Schulze","name":"Schulze, Christina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Eunice","key":"saxtofteunicepau","last":"Saxtoft","name":"Saxtoft, Eunice","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Barbara Malene","key":"fischerbarbaramalenepau","last":"Fischer","locid":"a87f805a-ba44-45e2-b257-59a6f2976711","name":"Fischer, Barbara Malene","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kim Francis","key":"andersenkimfrancispau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Kim Francis","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39355209"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fnume.2024.1398773","issn":["26738880"],"journal":"Frontiers in Nuclear Medicine","paperid":"1398773","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Nuclear Medicine","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85197575046"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-057995b6-0e50-4ced-a354-03706ca1625e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"QUALIPAED—A retrospective quality control study evaluating pediatric long axial field-of-view low-dose FDG-PET/CT","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747374","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Sphingosine 1-phosphate (S1P) is a lysosphingolipid with antiatherogenic properties, but mechanisms underlying its effects remain unclear. We here investigated atherosclerosis development in cholesterol-rich diet–fed LDL receptor–deficient mice with high or low overexpression levels of S1P receptor 1 (S1P1) in macrophages. S1P1-overexpressing macrophages showed increased activity of transcription factors PU.1, interferon regulatory factor 8 (IRF8), and liver X receptor (LXR) and were skewed toward an M2-distinct phenotype characterized by enhanced production of IL-10, IL-1RA, and IL-5; increased ATP-binding cassette transporter A1– and G1–dependent cholesterol efflux; increased expression of MerTK and efferocytosis; and reduced apoptosis due to elevated B cell lymphoma 6 and Maf bZIP B. A similar macrophage phenotype was observed in mice administered S1P1-selective agonist KRP203. Mechanistically, the enhanced PU.1, IRF8, and LXR activity in S1P1-overexpressing macrophages led to downregulation of the cAMP-dependent PKA and activation of the signaling cascade encompassing protein kinases AKT and mTOR complex 1 as well as the late endosomal/lysosomal adaptor MAPK and mTOR activator 1. Atherosclerotic lesions in aortic roots and brachiocephalic arteries were profoundly or moderately reduced in mice with high and low S1P1 overexpression in macrophages, respectively. We conclude that S1P1 signaling polarizes macrophages toward an antiatherogenic functional phenotype and countervails the development of atherosclerosis in mice.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Potì, Francesco","Scalera, Enrica","Feuerborn, Renata","Fischer, Josephine","Arndt, Lilli","Varga, Georg","Pardali, Evangelia","Seidl, Matthias D.","Fobker, Manfred","Liebisch, Gerhard","Hesse, Bettina","Lukasz, Alexander H.","Rossaint, Jan","Kehrel, Beate E.","Rosenbauer, Frank","Renné, Thomas","Christoffersen, Christina","Simoni, Manuela","Burkhardt, Ralph","Nofer, Jerzy Roch"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-790115"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Ireland","Italy","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","Leipzig University","MarienHospital Osnabrück","Nephrology","Pharvaris GmbH","Royal College of Surgeons in Ireland","University of Hamburg","University of Modena and Reggio Emilia","University of Münster","University of Parma","University of Regensburg"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sphingosine 000000000001 phosphate receptor 000000000001 signaling in macrophages reduces atherosclerosis in ldl receptor deficient mice","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1172/jci.insight.158127","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-790115","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11665566","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85212939563","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39531328","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-359db0f5-045b-4094-874a-28825bbe9401"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BF3BAF80AF110E0CA8A90320197A0693"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1172/jci.insight.158127","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/416331859/Sphingosine_1_phosphate.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of parma","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Parma","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of modena and reggio emilia","loc":["Italy"