{"abstract":"We performed a systematic evaluation of the diagnostic performance of LAFOV PET/CT with increasing acquisition time. The first 100 oncologic adult patients referred for 3 MBq/kg 2-[18F]fluoro-2-deoxy-D-glucose PET/CT on the Siemens Biograph Vision Quadra were included. A standard imaging protocol of 10 min was used and scans were reconstructed at 30 s, 60 s, 90 s, 180 s, 300 s, and 600 s. Paired comparisons of quantitative image noise, qualitative image quality, lesion detection, and lesion classification were performed. Image noise (n = 50, 34 women) was acceptable according to the current standard of care (coefficient-of-varianceref < 0.15) after 90 s and improved significantly with increasing acquisition time (PB < 0.001). The same was seen in observer rankings (PB < 0.001). Lesion detection (n = 100, 74 women) improved significantly from 30 s to 90 s (PB < 0.001), 90 s to 180 s (PB = 0.001), and 90 s to 300 s (PB = 0.002), while lesion classification improved from 90 s to 180 s (PB < 0.001), 180 s to 300 s (PB = 0.021), and 90 s to 300 s (PB < 0.001). We observed improved image quality, lesion detection, and lesion classification with increasing acquisition time while maintaining a total scan time of less than 5 min, which demonstrates a potential clinical benefit. Based on these results we recommend a standard imaging acquisition protocol for LAFOV PET/CT of minimum 180 s to maximum 300 s after injection of 3 MBq/kg 2-[18F]fluoro-2-deoxy-D-glucose.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Honoré d’Este, Sabrina","Andersen, Flemming Littrup","Andersen, Julie Bjerglund","Jakobsen, Annika Loft","Sanchez Saxtoft, Eunice","Schulze, Christina","Hansen, Naja Liv","Andersen, Kim Francis","Reichkendler, Michala Holm","Højgaard, Liselotte","Fischer, Barbara Malene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-721812"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","King's College London"],"keyword":["Image quality","Lesion detection","PET CT","Quadra","total body PET","whole body PET"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"potential clinical impact of lafov pet ct a systematic evaluation of image quality and lesion detection","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/diagnostics13213295","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-721812","identifier":[{"id":"85176440754","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10650426","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37958190","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c5f31b38-401a-4dca-a6b0-13bd57e23158"],"keyword":["PET-CT","image quality","lesion detection","long-axial field-of-view (LAFOV)","quadra","total-body PET","whole-body PET"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C94B5A88F56E0924BD473054E34FB3D4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/374645666/diagnostics_13_03295_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/diagnostics13213295","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, No speciality"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"king s college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"King's College London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sabrina","key":"honorédestesabrinapau","last":"Honoré d’Este","name":"Honoré d’Este, Sabrina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Flemming Littrup","key":"andersenflemminglittruppau","last":"Andersen","locid":"abbdc93c-3b5b-4a18-a96f-3be1e9e7da09","name":"Andersen, Flemming Littrup","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Julie Bjerglund","key":"andersenjuliebjerglundpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Julie Bjerglund","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Annika Loft","key":"jakobsenannikaloftpau","last":"Jakobsen","name":"Jakobsen, Annika Loft","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Eunice","key":"sanchezsaxtofteunicepau","last":"Sanchez Saxtoft","name":"Sanchez Saxtoft, Eunice","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"schulzechristinapau","last":"Schulze","name":"Schulze, Christina","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Naja Liv","key":"hansennajalivpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Naja Liv","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kim Francis","key":"andersenkimfrancispau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Kim Francis","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michala Holm","key":"reichkendlermichalaholmpau","last":"Reichkendler","name":"Reichkendler, Michala Holm","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Liselotte","key":"højgaardliselottepau","last":"Højgaard","locid":"fc298245-aff