{"abstract":"Acetogens have the ability to fixate carbon during fermentation by employing the Wood-Ljungdahl pathway (WLP), which is highly conserved across Bacteria and Archaea. In a previous study, product stoichometries in galacturonate-limited, anaerobic enrichment cultures of “Candidatus Galacturonibacter soehngenii,” from a novel genus within the Lachnospiraceae, suggested the simultaneous operation of a modified Entner-Doudoroff pathway for galacturonate fermentation and a WLP for acetogenesis. However, a draft metagenome-assembled genome (MAG) based on short reads did not reveal homologs of genes encoding a canonical WLP carbon-monoxide-dehydrogenase/acetyl-Coenzyme A synthase (CODH/ACS) complex. In this study, NaH13CO3 fed to chemostat-grown, galacturonate-limited enrichment cultures of “Ca. G. soehngenii” was shown to be incorporated into acetate. Preferential labeling of the carboxyl group of acetate was consistent with acetogenesis via a WLP in which the methyl group of acetate was predominately derived from formate. This interpretation was further supported by high transcript levels of a putative pyruvate-formate lyase gene and very low transcript levels of a candidate gene for formate dehydrogenase. Reassembly of the “Ca. G. soehngenii” MAG with support from long-read nanopore sequencing data produced a single-scaffold MAG, which confirmed the absence of canonical CODH/ACS-complex genes homologs. However, high CO-dehydrogenase activities were measured in cell extracts of “Ca. G. soehngenii” enrichment cultures, contradicting the absence of corresponding homologs in the MAG. Based on the highly conserved amino-acid motif associated with anaerobic Ni-CO dehydrogenase proteins, a novel candidate was identified which could be responsible for the observed activities. These results demonstrate operation of an acetogenic pathway, most probably as a yet unresolved variant of the Wood-Ljungdahl pathway, in anaerobic, galacturonate-limited cultures of “Ca. G. soehngenii.”","author_count":8,"contributors":["Valk, Laura Christina","Diender, Martijn","Stouten, Gerben R.","Petersen, Jette Fischer","Nielsen, Per Halkjær","Dueholm, Morten Simonsen","Pronk, Jack T.","van Loosdrecht, Mark C.M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-106475"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Valk, Laura Christina"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology","Wageningen University & Research"],"keyword":["Acetogenesis","C labeling","Wood Ljungdahl pathway"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"i candidatus i galacturonibacter soehngenii shows acetogenic catabolism of galacturonic acid but lacks a canonical carbon monoxide dehydrogenase acetyl coa synthase complex","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2020.00063","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research was supported by the SIAM Gravitation Grant 024.002.002, the Netherlands Organisation for Scientific Research."],"id":"S01-000.00-106475","identifier":[{"id":"85079495731","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-c27d0873-2936-4a65-b47c-6ec160338b80"],"keyword":["C-labeling","Wood-Ljungdahl pathway","acetogenesis","chemostat enrichment culture","meta-transcriptomics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0BA9DF5784DC99EE8F95E95BA298A044"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2020.00063","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/400448967/fmicb_11_00063.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"delft university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Delft University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"wageningen university research","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Wageningen University & Research","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura C.","key":"valkpau","last":"Valk","locid":"00e6eec6-c99a-4dd6-86f6-59eb7d57ad35","name":"Valk, Laura Christina","name_org":"Valk, Laura C.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Martijn","key":"dienderpau","last":"Diender","name":"Diender, Martijn","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gerben R.","key":"stoutenpau","last":"Stouten","name":"Stouten, Gerben R.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jette F.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"8c6830b5-cb42-4d8a-9f78-55910501bb2a","name":"Petersen, Jette Fischer","name_org":"Petersen, Jette F.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per H.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8321dd0d-5e0c-4334-81a7-ece0b4b66f4c","name":"Nielsen, Per Halkjær","name_org":"Nielsen, Per H.","orcid":"0000-0002-6402-1877","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten S.","key":"dueholmpau","last":"Dueholm","locid":"0824b5d0-8995-42b9-9df4-6e9996430c39","name":"Dueholm, Morten Simonsen","name_org":"Dueholm, Morten S.","orcid":"0000-0003-4135-2670","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jack T.","key":"pronkpau","last":"Pronk","name":"Pronk, Jack T.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark C.M.","key":"vanloosdrechtpau","last":"van Loosdrecht","name":"van Loosdrecht, Mark C.M.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fmicb.2020.00063","issn":["1664302X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Microbiology","paperid":"63","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Microbiology","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85079495731"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c27d0873-2936-4a65-b47c-6ec160338b80"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"“<i>Candidatus </i>Galacturonibacter soehngenii” Shows Acetogenic Catabolism of Galacturonic Acid but Lacks a Canonical Carbon Monoxide Dehydrogenase/Acetyl-CoA Synthase Complex","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-106475","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Key homeostatic functions are regulated in a diurnal manner and a miss-alignment of such rhythms is believed to contribute to the pathophysiology of several diseases. Signaling sphingolipids (SLs) in plasma such as sphingosine 1-phosphate control lymphocytic trafficking, vascular reactivity and platelet activity, physiological functions all of which display a diurnal rhythm themselves. However, the rhythmicity of SL metabolism in plasma and its potential causes have not been sufficiently investigated so far. Therefore, we analyzed blood of mice and healthy adult human subjects by targeted tandem mass-spectrometry at different time points. In order to investigate the influence of the synchronizing hormone melatonin, we compared melatonin proficient C3H/HeN wildtype mice (C3H) with melatonin receptor-1/2 double knockout mice (MT1/2−/−) and melatonin deficient C57BL/6J mice. We found a strong upregulation of plasma S1P with the beginning of the light period in C3H but not in MT1/2−/− or C57BL/6J mice. Accordingly, our study revealed an upregulation of sphingosine 1-phosphate (S1P d18:1) and sphinganine 1-phosphate (S1P d18:0) with the beginning of the light period in humans. Furthermore, plasma S1P d18:1 and S1P d18:0 were inversely correlated with the respective concentrations in platelets, pointing to a possible involvement of platelet SL metabolism. In humans, the diurnal rhythm of SLs was not associated with changes of SL-binding proteins or counts of cellular SL sources. Overall, this study indicates a physiological rhythmicity of plasma and platelet SL metabolism, likely mediated by melatonin, with potentially important implications for physiological diurnal rhythms and the regulation of SL metabolism and its functions.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Brunkhorst, Robert","Pfeilschifter, Waltraud","Rajkovic, Natasa","Pfeffer, Martina","Fischer, Claudia","Korf, Horst Werner","Christoffersen, Christina","Trautmann, Sandra","Thomas, Dominique","Pfeilschifter, Josef","Koch, Alexander"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-428581"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Goethe University Frankfurt"],"keyword":["Blood","Melatonin","Sphingolipids","Sphingosine 1 phosphate"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diurnal regulation of sphingolipids in blood","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85059162829&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-428581","identifier":[{"id":"30557628","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85059162829","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3af08aa3-b358-4faa-af9a-40d35fb82f04"],"keyword":["Blood","Melatonin","Sphingolipids","Sphingosine 1-phosphate"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DFE47823A78B57257C62963B6F26754C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"goethe university frankfurt","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Goethe University Frankfurt","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Robert","key":"brunkhorstrobertpau","last":"Brunkhorst","name":"Brunkhorst, Robert","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Waltraud","key":"pfeilschifterwaltraudpau","last":"Pfeilschifter","name":"Pfeilschifter, Waltraud","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Natasa","key":"rajkovicnatasapau","last":"Rajkovic","name":"Rajkovic, Natasa","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martina","key":"pfeffermartinapau","last":"Pfeffer","name":"Pfeffer, Martina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Claudia","key":"fischerclaudiapau","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, Claudia","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Horst Werner","key":"korfhorstwernerpau","last":"Korf","name":"Korf, Horst Werner","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenchristinapau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"7f6ac9b3-a8ee-401d-8c45-dc0bf731314a","name":"Christoffersen, Christina","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sandra","key":"trautmannsandrapau","last":"Trautmann","name":"Trautmann, Sandra","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dominique","key":"thomasdominiquepau","last":"Thomas","name":"Thomas, Dominique","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Josef","key":"pfeilschifterjosefpau","last":"Pfeilschifter","name":"Pfeilschifter, Josef","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Alexander","key":"kochalexanderpau","last":"Koch","name":"Koch, Alexander","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30557628"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.bbalip.2018.12.001","issn":["13881981","18792618"],"issn_org":["13881981"],"issue":"3","journal":"BBA - Molecular and Cell Biology of Lipids","pages":"304-311","status":"p","title":"BBA - Molecular and Cell Biology of Lipids","title_org":"Biochimica et Biophysica Acta - Molecular and Cell Biology of Lipids","volume":"1864"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85059162829"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3af08aa3-b358-4faa-af9a-40d35fb82f04"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Diurnal regulation of sphingolipids in blood","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-428581","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Moderately increased plasma ferritin, as a biomarker of iron overload, has been associated with higher rates of cardiovascular death and heart failure. However, the association of moderately increased plasma ferritin with risk of atrial fibrillation in the general population is unknown. METHODS: We examined the association of plasma ferritin concentrations with risk of atrial fibrillation and heart failure in metaanalyses of 35799 men and women from 3 studies of the Danish general population: the Copenhagen City Heart Study, the Danish General Suburban Population Study, and the Copenhagen General Population Study. RESULTS: Multivariable adjusted fixed effects odds ratios for atrial fibrillation were 1.23 (95% CI, 1.05-1.44; P = 0.005) in men for ferritin concentration ≥300 μg/L vs <300 μg/L, 1.13 (95% CI, 0.93-1.38; P = 0.22) in women for ≥200 μg/L vs <200 μg/L, and 1.19 (95% CI, 1.06-1.35; P = 0.005) in both sexes combined (Psex interaction = 0.52). Corresponding fixed effects odds ratios for heart failure were 1.16 (95% CI, 0.98-1.37; P = 0.08) in men, 0.86 (95% CI, 0.67-1.10; P = 0.23) in women, and 1.05 (95% CI, 0.91-1.21; P = 0.45) in both sexes combined (Psex interaction = 0.05). Multivariable adjusted fixed effects odds ratio for atrial fibrillation per step increase in ferritin concentrations was 1.13 (95% CI, 1.06-1.21; Ptrend = 0.0005) in both sexes combined (Psex interaction = 0.59); the corresponding value for heart failure was 1.03 (95% CI, 0.95-1.11; Ptrend = 0.47) (Psex interaction = 0.08). In sensitivity analyses, there was no evidence of U-shaped relationships between plasma ferritin concentrations and risk of atrial fibrillation or heart failure in men or women. CONCLUSIONS: Increased ferritin concentration is associated with increased risk of atrial fibrillation in the general population.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Mikkelsen, Lise Fischer","Nordestgaard, Børge G","Schnohr, Peter","Ellervik, Christina"],"cuid":["S02-099.35-016004"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard University"],"keyword":["Association","CARBOXYMALTOSE","Deficiency","Inflammation","Iron overload","Mediterranean diet","Mendelian randomization","Metaanalysis","Serum ferritin"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"increased ferritin concentration and risk of atrial fibrillation and heart failure in men and women three studies of the danish general population including 000000035799 individuals","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85059495023","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.35-016004","identifier":[{"id":"85059495023","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000454688100029","type":"wos"},{"id":"30459161","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-2e9b8588-9fb5-4d8e-831f-0bc027470aae","ku-7959a7f7-5fdc-4a1c-bc70-953d286b85ba"],"keyword":["ASSOCIATION","CARBOXYMALTOSE","DEFICIENCY","HEREDITARY HEMOCHROMATOSIS","INFLAMMATION","IRON-OVERLOAD","MEDITERRANEAN DIET","MENDELIAN RANDOMIZATION","METAANALYSIS","SERUM FERRITIN"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8F78184C1CD5678538CB2C6DFF2E3821"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Diagnostisk Center, Universitetsklinik for Innovative Patientforløb, Silkeborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lise Fischer","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","locid":"df925d72-f143-41b2-8158-93f35fcf7b46","name":"Mikkelsen, Lise Fischer","orcid":"0000-0003-4440-1175","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Børge G.","key":"nordestgaardpau","last":"Nordestgaard","locid":"733103b5-ddc2-416f-a686-48e694154a82","name":"Nordestgaard, Børge G","name_org":"Nordestgaard, Børge G.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"schnohrpau","last":"Schnohr","name":"Schnohr, Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Christina","key":"ellervikpau","last":"Ellervik","locid":"f08e5172-d3cf-4e0a-a733-6a450b16075a","name":"Ellervik, Christina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30459161"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1373/clinchem.2018.292763","issn":["00099147","15308561"],"issn_org":["00099147"],"issue":"1","journal":"Clinical Chemistry","pages":"180-188","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Clinical Chemistry","volume":"65"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85059495023"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2e9b8588-9fb5-4d8e-831f-0bc027470aae","ku-7959a7f7-5fdc-4a1c-bc70-953d286b85ba"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Increased Ferritin Concentration and Risk of Atrial Fibrillation and Heart Failure in Men and Women : Three Studies of the Danish General Population Including 35799 Individuals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.35-016004","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The purpose of the European Stroke Organisation-Karolinska Stroke Update Conference is to provide updates on recent stroke therapy research and to give an opportunity for the participants to discuss how these results may be implemented into clinical routine. The meeting started 22 years ago as Karolinska Stroke Update, but since 2014 it is a joint conference with European Stroke Organisation. Importantly, it provides a platform for discussion on the European Stroke Organisation guidelines process and on recommendations to the European Stroke Organisation guidelines committee on specific topics. By this, it adds a direct influence from stroke professionals otherwise not involved in committees and work groups on the guideline procedure. The discussions at the conference may also inspire new guidelines when motivated. The topics raised at the meeting are selected by the scientific programme committee mainly based on recent important scientific publications. This year's European Stroke Organisation-Karolinska Stroke Update Meeting was held in Stockholm on 11-13 November 2018. There were 11 scientific sessions discussed in the meeting including two short sessions. Each session except the short sessions produced a consensus statement (Full version with background, issues, conclusions and references are published as web-material and at www.eso-karolinska.org and http://eso-stroke.org) and recommendations which were prepared by a writing committee consisting of session chair(s), scientific secretary and speakers. These statements were presented to the 250 participants of the meeting. In the open meeting, general participants commented on the consensus statement and recommendations and the final document were adjusted based on the discussion from the general participants Recommendations (grade of evidence) were graded according to the 1998 Karolinska Stroke Update meeting with regard to the strength of evidence. Grade A Evidence: Strong support from randomised controlled trials and statistical reviews (at least one randomised controlled trial plus one statistical review). Grade B Evidence: Support from randomised controlled trials and statistical reviews (one randomised controlled trial or one statistical review). Grade C Evidence: No reasonable support from randomised controlled trials, recommendations based on small randomised and/or non-randomised controlled trials evidence.","author_count":47,"contributors":["Ahmed, Niaz","Audebert, Heinrich","Turc, Guillaume","Cordonnier, Charlotte","Christensen, Hanne","Sacco, Simona","Sandset, Else Charlotte","Ntaios, George","Charidimou, Andreas","Toni, Danilo","Pristipino, Christian","Köhrmann, Martin","Kuramatsu, Joji B","Thomalla, Götz","Mikulik, Robert","Ford, Gary A","Martí-Fàbregas, Joan","Fischer, Urs","Thoren, Magnus","Lundström, Erik","Rinkel, Gabriel Je","van der Worp, H Bart","Matusevicius, Marius","Tsivgoulis, Georgios","Milionis, Haralampos","Rubiera, Marta","Hart, Robert","Moreira, Tiago","Lantz, Maria","Sjöstrand, Christina","Andersen, Grethe","Schellinger, Peter","Kostulas, Konstantinos","Sunnerhagen, Katharina Stibrant","Keselman, Boris","Korompoki, Eleni","Purrucker, Jan","Khatri, Pooja","Whiteley, William","Berge, Eivind","Mazya, Michael","Dippel, Diederik Wj","Mustanoja, Satu","Rasmussen, Mads","Söderqvist, Åsa Kuntze","Escudero-Martínez, Irene","Steiner, Thorsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-133805"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Intracerebral haemorrhage","Ischaemic stroke","Oral anticoagulation","Patent foramen ovale","Prehospital","Stroke","Thrombectomy","Thrombolysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"consensus statements and recommendations from the eso karolinska stroke update conference stockho