{"abstract":"Purpose: Phenotype information is crucial for the interpretation of genomic variants. So far it has only been accessible for bioinformatics workflows after encoding into clinical terms by expert dysmorphologists. Methods: Here, we introduce an approach driven by artificial intelligence that uses portrait photographs for the interpretation of clinical exome data. We measured the value added by computer-assisted image analysis to the diagnostic yield on a cohort consisting of 679 individuals with 105 different monogenic disorders. For each case in the cohort we compiled frontal photos, clinical features, and the disease-causing variants, and simulated multiple exomes of different ethnic backgrounds. Results: The additional use of similarity scores from computer-assisted analysis of frontal photos improved the top 1 accuracy rate by more than 20–89% and the top 10 accuracy rate by more than 5–99% for the disease-causing gene. Conclusion: Image analysis by deep-learning algorithms can be used to quantify the phenotypic similarity (PP4 criterion of the American College of Medical Genetics and Genomics guidelines) and to advance the performance of bioinformatics pipelines for exome analysis.","author_count":61,"contributors":["Hsieh, Tzung Chien","Mensah, Martin A.","Pantel, Jean T.","Aguilar, Dione","Bar, Omri","Bayat, Allan","Becerra-Solano, Luis","Bentzen, Heidi B.","Biskup, Saskia","Borisov, Oleg","Braaten, Oivind","Ciaccio, Claudia","Coutelier, Marie","Cremer, Kirsten","Danyel, Magdalena","Daschkey, Svenja","Eden, Hilda David","Devriendt, Koenraad","Wilson, Sandra","Douzgou, Sofia","Đukić, Dejan","Ehmke, Nadja","Fauth, Christine","Fischer-Zirnsak, Björn","Fleischer, Nicole","Gabriel, Heinz","Graul-Neumann, Luitgard","Gripp, Karen W.","Gurovich, Yaron","Gusina, Asya","Haddad, Nechama","Hajjir, Nurulhuda","Hanani, Yair","Hertzberg, Jakob","Hoertnagel, Konstanze","Howell, Janelle","Ivanovski, Ivan","Kaindl, Angela","Kamphans, Tom","Kamphausen, Susanne","Karimov, Catherine","Kathom, Hadil","Keryan, Anna","Knaus, Alexej","Köhler, Sebastian","Kornak, Uwe","Lavrov, Alexander","Leitheiser, Maximilian","Lyon, Gholson J.","Fagerberg, Christina","Robinson, Peter Nick","Rosnev, Stanislav","Rudnik, Sabine","Rudolf, Gorazd","Schatz, Ulrich","Schossig, Anna","Schubach, Max","Shanoon, Or","Sheridan, Eamonn","Smirin-Yosef, Pola","Spielmann, Malte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-621633"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, Central","America, North","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bulgaria","Germany","Israel","Italy","Mexico","Norway","Russia","Slovenia","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["AUSL-IRCCS Reggio Emilia","All Global Affiliations","Ariel University","Berlin Institute of Health","CeGaT GmbH","Charité - University Medicine Berlin","Children's Hospital Los Angeles","Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory","Department of Genetic Medicine, Manchester University NHS Foundation Trust, Manchester, United Kingdom.","Eberhard Karls University of Tübingen","FDNA Inc.","Foundation IRCCS Carlo Besta Neurological Institute","GeneTalk","Heinrich Heine University Düsseldorf","Jackson Laboratory","Lineagen, Inc.","Medical University Sofia","Medical University of Innsbruck","Monterrey Institute of Technology and Higher Education","National Research and Applied Medicine Centre ‘Mother and Child’’","Nemours Children's Health System","Otto von Guericke University Magdeburg","Russian Academy of Sciences","Unidad de Investigación Médica en Medicina Reproductiva","University Hospital Bonn","University Medical Center Hamburg-Eppendorf","University Medical Centre Ljubljana","University of Bonn","University of Leeds","University of Leuven","University of Manchester","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Computer vision","Deep learning","Variant prioritization"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"O