{"abstract":"Context Human land use intensified over the last century and simultaneously, extreme weather events have become more frequent. However, little is known about the interplay between habitat structure, direct short-term weather effects and indirect seasonal effects on animal space use and behavior. Objectives We used the European hare (Lepus europaeus) as model to investigate how habitat structure and weather conditions affect habitat selection and home range size, predictors for habitat quality and energetic requirements. Methods Using > 100,000 GPS positions of 60 hares in three areas in Denmark and Germany, we analyzed habitat selection and home range size in response to seasonally changing habitat structure, measured as vegetation height and agricultural field size, and weather. We compared daily and monthly home ranges to disentangle between direct short-term weather effects and indirect seasonal effects of climate. Results Habitat selection and home range size varied seasonally as a response to changing habitat structure, potentially affecting the availability of food and shelter. Overall, habitat structure and seasonality were more important in explaining hare habitat selection and home range size compared to direct weather conditions. Nevertheless, hares adjusted habitat selection and daily home range size in response to temperature, wind speed and humidity, possibly in response to thermal constrains and predation risk. Conclusions For effective conservation, habitat heterogeneity should be increased, e.g. by reducing agricultural field sizes and the implementation of set-asides that provide both forage and shelter, especially during the colder months of the year.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Mayer, Martin","Ullmann, Wiebke","Heinrich, Rebecca","Fischer, Christina","Blaum, Niels","Sunde, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-177528"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Technical University of Munich","University of Potsdam"],"keyword":["European hare","GPS","Habitat selection","Home range","Lepus europaeus","Weather"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"seasonal effects of habitat structure and weather on the habitat selection and home range size of a mammal in agricultural landscapes","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85070320867","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-177528","identifier":[{"id":"85070320867","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000490066800007","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-548237a5-b6da-4e5a-a1b7-1fb36b995c27"],"keyword":["European hare","GPS","Habitat selection","Home range","Lepus europaeus","Weather"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3E4A03E39610A54F6141E5B2E3646E7D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Wildlife Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of potsdam","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Potsdam","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"mayerpau","last":"Mayer","locid":"bfc4db27-d06d-4e2a-8e51-272b4dbf95de","name":"Mayer, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-9905-3625","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wiebke","key":"ullmannpau","last":"Ullmann","name":"Ullmann, Wiebke","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rebecca","key":"heinrichpau","last":"Heinrich","name":"Heinrich, Rebecca","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, Christina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"blaumpau","last":"Blaum","name":"Blaum, Niels","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"sundepau","last":"Sunde","locid":"3a9b01f6-a55e-40f0-9f76-9f8bb4d5d466","name":"Sunde, Peter","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10980-019-00878-9","issn":["09212973","15729761"],"issn_org":["09212973"],"issue":"10","journal":"Landscape Ecology","pages":"2279-2294","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media BV","publisher_org":"Springer Science and Business Media B.V.","status":"p","title":"Landscape Ecology","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85070320867"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-548237a5-b6da-4e5a-a1b7-1fb36b995c27"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Seasonal effects of habitat structure and weather on the habitat selection and home range size of a mammal in agricultural landscapes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-177528","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: Calcium electroporation is a novel cancer treatment, which combines temporary cell permeability from electroporation with a high influx of calcium intracellularly resulting in cancer cell necrosis. Methods: A phase I trial performing calcium electroporation on 6 patients suffering from recurrent head and neck cancer. In general anesthesia, intratumoral calcium injections were followed by electroporation. Safety was monitored by adverse events registration, serum Ca2+, ECG, and pain scores. Tumor response was measured on PET/MRI scans. Results: Procedures were performed without complications. No serious adverse events, signs of hypercalcemia, or cardiac arrhythmias were observed. Two months post-treatment tumor responses on MRI: three partial responses, one stable disease, and two progression. Responses on PET: one partial metabolic disease, four with stable metabolic disease, and one not evaluable. One patient was without clinical evidence of disease after 12 months of observation. Conclusion: Calcium electroporation is feasible and safe in head and neck tumors. Clinical responses were observed in three of six patients, warranting further studies. Level of Evidence: Level 4.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Plaschke, Christina Caroline","Gehl, Julie","Johannesen, Helle Hjorth","Fischer, Barbara Malene","Kjaer, Andreas","Lomholt, Anne Fog","Wessel, Irene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-485568"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"calcium electroporation for recurrent head and neck cancer a clinical phase i study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/lio2.233","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-485568","identifier":[{"id":"30828619","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85067429315","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6383303","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-9a22005c-8012-4d0c-8adc-a9ea78f24227"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FF45FB05448D3759F81678E30195FFF0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/lio2.233","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/236271124/Plaschke_et_al_2019_Laryngoscope_Investigative_Otolaryngology_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Oncology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christina Caroline","key":"plaschkepau","last":"Plaschke","name":"Plaschke, Christina Caroline","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Julie","key":"gehlpau","last":"Gehl","locid":"39c5bc6b-5473-4041-8f1e-19bb85da