{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: To examine whether the quality of the patient-physician relationship, assessed by the general practitioner (GP) and the patient, associates with GPs' use of gut feeling (GF) in cancer diagnosis. DESIGN: Cross-sectional questionnaire survey of cancer patients and their GPs. SETTING: Danish primary care. PARTICIPANTS: Newly diagnosed cancer patients and their GPs. Patients completed a questionnaire and provided the name of the GP to whom they have presented their symptoms. The named GP subsequently received a questionnaire. PRIMARY AND SECONDARY OUTCOME MEASURES: GPs' use of GF in the diagnostic process for the particular patient. GPs who answered that they used their GF 'to a high degree' or 'to a very high degree' were categorised as 'used their GF to a great extent'. GPs who answered that they used their GF 'to some degree', 'to a limited degree' or 'not at all' were categorised as 'limited or no use of GF'. RESULTS: GPs were less likely to use GF when they assessed relational aspects of the patient encounter as difficult compared with less difficult (OR=0.67; 95% CI 0.46 to 0.97). The physician-reported level of empathy was positively associated with use of GF (OR=2.60; 95% CI 1.60 to 4.22). The lower use of GF in difficult encounters was not modified by level of empathy. CONCLUSIONS: Experiencing relational aspects of patient encounter as difficult acted as a barrier for the use of GF in cancer diagnosis. Although physician-rated empathy increased use of GF, high empathy did not dissolve the low use of GF in difficult encounters. As diagnosis of cancer is a key challenge in primary care, it is important that GPs are aware that the sensitivity of cancer-related GF is compromised by a difficult patient-physician relationship.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Pedersen, Anette Fischer","Andersen, Christina Maar","Ingeman, Mads Lind","Vedsted, Peter"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-013494"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adult oncology","Mental health","Primary care","Public health"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patient physician relationship and use of gut feeling in cancer diagnosis in primary care a cross sectional survey of patients and their general practitioners","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2018-027288","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-013494","identifier":[{"id":"85068875362","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31289073","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6629394","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000485269700333","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-0c4750a0-74d4-40ff-907c-3803cbd8ad60","sdu-3823ef09-eb6d-4546-aa59-f39b9d47e47c"],"keyword":["adult oncology","mental health","primary care","public health"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CB77B097997F5F779496A9719B153212"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2018-027288","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/152367583/Patient_physician_relationship_and_use_of_gut_feeling_in_cancer_diagnosis_in_primary_care.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Forskningsenheden for Almen Praksis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Psychology","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Psychology, INSIDE"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anette Fischer","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"82636514-da9f-4741-a33d-1555d4730827","name":"Pedersen, Anette Fischer","orcid":"0000-0003-0253-3671","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Maar","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"8f5fe69c-4e0b-4da7-8da2-c9cb54ebbda6","name":"Andersen, Christina Maar","orcid":"0000-0001-8008-6729","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Lind","key":"ingemanpau","last":"Ingeman","locid":"e2e19f92-ba3a-4d1a-8753-cfbec6562af9","name":"Ingeman, Mads Lind","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"vedstedpau","last":"Vedsted","locid":"bb00d9e7-866c-4f04-8e3b-a71c913c39b0","name":"Vedsted, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-2113-5599","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31289073"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmjopen-2018-027288","issn":["20446055"],"issue":"7","journal":"BMJ Open","paperid":"e027288","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ Open","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85068875362"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0c4750a0-74d4-40ff-907c-3803cbd8ad60","sdu-3823ef09-eb6d-4546-aa59-f39b9d47e47c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Patient-physician relationship and use of gut feeling in cancer diagnosis in primary care : a cross-sectional survey of patients and their general practitioners","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-013494","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"It is well known that sepsis and inflammation reduce male fertility. Within the testis, toll-like receptor 3 (TLR3) is constitutively expressed and recognizes double-stranded RNA (dsRNA) from viruses, degraded bacteria, damaged tissues and necrotic cells. To characterize the potential role of TLR3 in response to testicular infections, its expression and downstream signaling were investigated upon challenge with lipopolysaccharides (LPS) in two mouse strains that differ in their immuno-competence regarding T cell-regulated immunity. Thereto, Balb/c and Foxn1nu mice were randomized into six interventional groups treated with either i.v. application of saline or LPS followed by 20 min, 5 h 30 min and 18 h of observation and two sham-treated control groups. LPS administration induced a significant stress response; the amplification was manifested for TLR3 and interleukin 6 (IL6) mRNA in the impaired testis 5 h 30 min after LPS injection. TLR3 immunostaining revealed that TLR3 was primarily localized in spermatocytes. The TLR3 expression displayed different temporal dynamics between both mouse strains. However, immunofluorescence staining indicated only punctual interferon regulatory factor 3 (IRF3) expression upon LPS treatment along with minor alterations in interferon beta (IFN beta) mRNA expression. Induction of acute inflammation was closely followed by a significant shift of the Bax/Bcl2 ratio to pro-apoptotic signaling accompanied by augmented TUNEL-positive cells 18 h after LPS injection with again differing patterns in both mouse strains. In conclusion, this study shows the involvement of TLR3 in response to LPS-induced testicular inflammation in immuno-competent and -incompetent mice, yet lacking transmission into its signaling pathway.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Nejsum, Lene Niemann","Piec, Adrian","Fijak, Monika","Ernstsen, Christina V","Fischer, Dania","Maier, Thorsten J","Kinscherf, Ralf","Hofmann, Rainer","Urbschat, Anja"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-230271"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Goethe University Frankfurt","Justus Liebig University Giessen","University of Marburg"],"keyword":["Activation","Apoptosis","Germ Cells","Innate immune responses","Interleukin 6","Lipopolysaccharide","Lymphocytes","Mutations","RNA","Recognition","Sepsis","Sertoli Cells","TLR3","Testis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"systemic lps induces toll like receptor 000000000003 tlr000000000003 expression and apoptosis in testicular mouse tissue","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85064443895","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-230271","identifier":[{"id":"85064443895","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000487075100011","type":"wos"},{"id":"30989399","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b0f30065-89eb-49e3-abd6-693770042076"],"keyword":["ACTIVATION","Apoptosis","GERM-CELLS","INNATE IMMUNE-RESPONSES","INTERLEUKIN-6","LYMPHOCYTES","Lipopolysaccharide","MUTATIONS","RECOGNITION","RNA","SERTOLI-CELLS","Sepsis","TLR3","Testis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2DE124824E5AB9BFD11805143693E82A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of marburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Marburg","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"justus liebig university giessen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Justus Liebig University Giessen","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"goethe university frankfurt","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Goethe University Frankfurt","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene N","key":"nejsumpau","last":"Nejsum","locid":"1dd4a525-1bc6-4922-b52d-eeb6ef9ffb44","name":"Nejsum, Lene Niemann","name_org":"Nejsum, Lene N","orcid":"0000-0003-4368-8821","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Adrian","key":"piecpau","last":"Piec","name":"Piec, Adrian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Monika","key":"fijakpau","last":"Fijak","name":"Fijak, Monika","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christina V","key":"ernstsenpau","last":"Ernstsen","locid":"7098f536-2cce-4b1c-b5ee-22ad70f7b2be","name":"Ernstsen, Christina V","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Dania","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, Dania","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thorsten J","key":"maierpau","last":"Maier","locid":"76395e20-880e-4d7b-8037-d43b8b1de607","name":"Maier, Thorsten J","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ralf","key":"kinscherfpau","last":"Kinscherf","name":"Kinscherf, Ralf","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rainer","key":"hofmannpau","last":"Hofmann","name":"Hofmann, Rainer","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anja","key":"urbschatpau","last":"Urbschat","locid":"3a301f28-3b7d-450c-8fbd-8aa3d861e402","name":"Urbschat, Anja","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30989399"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00441-019-03022-w","issn":["0302766X","14320878"],"issn_org":["0302766X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Cell and Tissue Research","pages":"143-154","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Cell and Tissue Research","volume":"378"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85064443895"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b0f30065-89eb-49e3-abd6-693770042076"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Systemic LPS induces toll-like receptor 3 (TLR3) expression and apoptosis in testicular mouse tissue","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-230271","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In medical human-robot interactions, trust plays an important role since for patients there may be more at stake than during other kinds of encounters with robots. In the current study, we address issues of trust in the interaction with a prototype of a therapeutic robot, the Universal RoboTrainer, in which the therapist records patient-specific tasks for the patient by means of kinesthetic guidance of the patients arm, which is connected to the robot. We carried out a user study with twelve pairs of participants who collaborate on recording a training program on the robot. We examine a) the degree with which participants identify the situation as uncomfortable or distressing, b) participants' own strategies to mitigate that stress, c) the degree to which the robot is held responsible for the problems occurring and the amount of agency ascribed to it, and d) when usability issues arise, what effect these have on participants' trust. We find signs of distress mostly in contexts with usability issues, as well as many verbal and kinesthetic mitigation strategies intuitively employed by the participants. Recommendations for robots to increase users' trust in kinesthetic interactions include the timely production of verbal cues that continuously confirm that everything is alright as well as increased contingency in the presentation of strategies for recovering from usability issues arising.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Weigelin, Bente Charlotte","Mathiesen, Mia","Nielsen, Christina","Fischer, Kerstin","Nielsen, Jacob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-594626"],"event":{"acronym":"RO-MAN","end":"2018-08-31","place":"Nanjing, cn","start":"2018-08-27","title":"RO-MAN 2018 - IEEE International Conference on Robot and Human Interactive Communication","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"trust in medical human robot interactions based on kinesthetic guidance","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85058076557","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-594626","identifier":[{"id":"85058076557","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-4ab02d31-3fb8-4442-92dc-0abb8f7b6865"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CCD6416606838B625D0993FCA5C06AE0"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente Charlotte","key":"weigelinbentecharlottepau","last":"Weigelin","locid":"e8e659cc-c764-47c4-bd0d-dc7ffe3e682f","name":"Weigelin, Bente Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-3892-4834","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mia","key":"mathiesenmiapau","last":"Mathiesen","name":"Mathiesen, Mia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"nielsenchristinapau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Christina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kerstin","key":"fischerkerstinpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"a963aa0b-6bfd-4dae-bc40-e51cf9da39b9","name":"Fischer, Kerstin","orcid":"0000-0003-1987-5344","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"nielsenjacobpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"bfca7bf8-41f7-4f6d-af41-38b9d20dbb8a","name":"Nielsen, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0002-5134-8950","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/roman.2018.8525677","eisbn":["9781538679807","9781538679791"],"isbn":["9781538679814"],"issn":["19449445"],"pages":"901-908","publisher":"IEEE","series":"Proceedings - IEEE International Workshop on Robot and Human Communication","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 27th IEEE International Symposium on Robot and Human Interactive Communication (RO-MAN)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058076557"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-4ab02d31-3fb8-4442-92dc-0abb8f7b6865"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Trust in Medical Human-Robot Interactions based on Kinesthetic Guidance","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-594626","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In cancer cells, cancer/testis (CT) antigens become epigenetically derepressed through DNA demethylation and constitute attractive targets for cancer immunotherapy. Here we report that activated CD4+ T helper cells treated with a DNA-demethylating agent express a broad repertoire of endogenous CT antigens and can be used as antigen-presenting cells to generate autologous cytotoxic T lymphocytes (CTLs) and natural killer cells. In vitro, activated CTLs induce HLA-restricted lysis of tumor cells of different histological types, as well as cells expressing single CT antigens. In a phase 1 trial of 25 patients with recurrent glioblastoma multiforme, cytotoxic lymphocytes homed to the tumor, with tumor regression ongoing in three patients for 14, 22, and 27 months, respectively. No treatment-related adverse effects were observed. This proof-of-principle study shows that tumor-reactive effector cells can be generated ex vivo by exposure to antigens induced by DNA demethylation, providing a novel, minimally invasive therapeutic strategy for treating cancer.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Kirkin, Alexei F.","Dzhandzhugazyan, Karine N.","Guldberg, Per","Fang, Johnny Jon","Andersen, Rikke S.","Dahl, Christina","Mortensen, Jann","Lundby, Tim","Wagner, Aase","Law, Ian","Broholm, Helle","Madsen, Line Bille","Lundell-Ek, Christer","Gjerstorff, Morten F.","Ditzel, Henrik J.","Jensen, Martin R.","Fischer, Walter"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-030349"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Kirkin, Alexei F."],"keyword":["Adult","Antigen Presenting Cells immunology","Antigens Neoplasm genetics","Brain Neoplasms genetics","DNA genetics","DNA methylation","Female","Glioblastoma genetics","Humans","Immunotherapy Adoptive","Male","Prospective Studies","T Lymphocytes Cytotoxic immunology","T Lymphocytes Helper Inducer immunology","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"adoptive cancer immunotherapy using dna demethylated t helper cells as antigen presenting cells","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-03217-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-030349","identifier":[{"id":"29511178","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85043244810","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5840134","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-f514d24a-a078-48a6-91c6-30639fb902a5","ku-4c776294-530f-46c1-8faf-77b1740a7a6b","sdu-09f7629a-7683-487f-93a0-cbb25e3f2f19"],"keyword":["Adult","Antigen-Presenting Cells/immunology","Antigens, Neoplasm/genetics","Brain Neoplasms/genetics","DNA Methylation","DNA/genetics","Female","Glioblastoma/genetics","Humans","Immunotherapy, Adoptive","Male","Prospective Studies","T-Lymphocytes, Cytotoxic/immunology","T-Lymphocytes, Helper-Inducer/immunology","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-4229540EE8E4A925DC30AE352B0FEB8F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/137627432/Adoptive_cancer_immunotherapy_using_DNA_demethylated_T_helper_cells_as_antigen_presenting_cells.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/216470762/s41467_018_03217_9.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-03217-9","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Department of Cancer and Inflammation Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Physiology and Nuclear Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Dep