{"abstract":"The aim of the study is to compare the efficacy of SPIO as a tracer in sentinel node biopsy (SNB) in breast cancer with Tc and patent blue in a multicentre prospective study and perform a meta-analysis of all published studies. It also aims to follow skin discoloration after SPIO injection and describe when and how it resolves. Totally 206 patients with early breast cancer were recruited. Tc and patent blue were administered in standard fashion. Patients were injected with SPIO (Sienna+) preoperatively. SNB was performed and detection rates were recorded for both methods. Skin discoloration was followed and documented postoperatively. Data extraction and subsequent meta-analysis of all previous studies were also performed. SN detection rates were similar between standard technique succeeded and SPIO both per patient (97.1 vs. 97.6 %, p = 0.76) as well as per node (91.3 vs. 93.3 %, p = 0.34), something which was not affected by the presence of malignancy. Concordance rates were also consistently high (98.0 % per patient and 95.9 % per node). Discoloring was present in 35.5 % of patients postoperatively, almost exclusively in breast conservation. It fades slowly and is still detectable in 8.6 % of patients after 15 months. Meta-analysis depicted similar detection rates (p = 0.71) and concordance rates (p = 0.82) per patient. However, it seems that SPIO is characterized by higher nodal retrieval (p < 0.001). SPIO is an effective method for the detection of SN in patients with breast cancer. It is comparable to the standard technique and seems to simplify logistics. Potential skin discoloration is something of consideration in patients planned for breast conservation.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Karakatsanis, Andreas","Christiansen, Peer","Fischer, Lone","Hedin, Christina","Pistioli, Lida","Sund, Malin","Rasmussen, Nils Ryegaard","Jørnsgård, Hjørdis","Tegnelius, Daniel","Eriksson, Staffan","Daskalakis, Kosmas","Wärnberg, Fredrik","Markopoulos, Christos J","Bergkvist, Leif"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-256985"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Breast cancer","Sentinel node","Super paramagnetic iron oxide"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the nordic sentimag trial a comparison of super paramagnetic iron oxide spio nanoparticles versus tc 000000000099 and patent blue in the detection of sentinel node sn in patients with breast cancer and a meta analysis of earlier studies","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84979642954","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-256985","identifier":[{"id":"84979642954","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27117158","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4875068","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-df9c1bc9-241a-43ad-b3c7-23cb3ed5bf49"],"keyword":["Breast cancer","Sentinel node","Super paramagnetic iron oxide"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3837D76F66CDE0754CE80A45E3518BDB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Plastic and Breast surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"karakatsanispau","last":"Karakatsanis","name":"Karakatsanis, Andreas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peer Michael","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"31f1ce54-ae25-4084-b4fc-798d3e0eb07d","name":"Christiansen, Peer","name_org":"Christiansen, Peer Michael","orcid":"0000-0003-2748-9240","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, Lone","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"hedinpau","last":"Hedin","name":"Hedin, Christina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lida","key":"pistiolipau","last":"Pistioli","name":"Pistioli, Lida","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Malin","key":"sundpau","last":"Sund","name":"Sund, Malin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nils Ryegaard","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Nils Ryegaard","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hjørdis","key":"jørnsgårdpau","last":"Jørnsgård","name":"Jørnsgård, Hjørdis","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"tegneliuspau","last":"Tegnelius","name":"Tegnelius, Daniel","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Staffan","key":"erikssonpau","last":"Eriksson","name":"Eriksson, Staffan","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kosmas","key":"daskalakispau","last":"Daskalakis","name":"Daskalakis, Kosmas","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Fredrik","key":"wärnbergpau","last":"Wärnberg","name":"Wärnberg, Fredrik","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christos J","key":"markopoulospau","last":"Markopoulos","name":"Markopoulos, Christos J","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Leif","key":"bergkvistpau","last":"Bergkvist","name":"Bergkvist, Leif","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27117158"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10549-016-3809-9","issn":["01676806","15737217"],"issn_org":["01676806"],"issue":"2","journal":"Breast Cancer Research and Treatment","pages":"281-294","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Breast Cancer Research and Treatment","volume":"157"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84979642954"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-df9c1bc9-241a-43ad-b3c7-23cb3ed5bf49"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The Nordic SentiMag trial : a comparison of super paramagnetic iron oxide (SPIO) nanoparticles versus Tc(99) and patent blue in the detection of sentinel node (SN) in patients with breast cancer and a meta-analysis of earlier studies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-256985","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The prolongation of cardiac repolarization (QT interval) has been investigated in studies of patients with secondary iron overload. However, no previous population-based study examining the effect of increased iron stores on QT interval prolongation has previously been undertaken. We tested the hypothesis that increased iron stores and haemochromatosis genotype (genetically increased iron stores) are associated with prolongation of the QT interval. We included 20 261 individuals from the Danish General Suburban Population Study and examined differences in QT interval according to ferritin concentration, transferrin saturation, iron concentration, transferrin concentration and haemochromatosis genotype (C282Y/C282Y). Furthermore, we performed a meta-analysis of case-control studies on thalassaemia major patients and QT interval. Age- and C-reactive protein-adjusted mean corrected QT (QTc) intervals for ferritin concentration ≥99% vs. ≥25-<50% percentile were 418·9 ms vs. 412·7 ms in men (P < 0·001) and 422·4 ms vs. 419·1 ms in women (P = 0·78). Corresponding values for transferrin saturation were 417·6 ms vs. 412·6 ms in men (P = 0·02) and 421·5 ms vs. 419·4 ms in women (P = 0·86). The associations were not explained by inflammation and haemochromatosis genotype was not associated with QT interval length. In conclusion, increased iron stores, independent of haemochromatosis genotype and inflammation, are associated with prolongation of the QTc interval in men. This is a novel finding. In addition, the meta-analysis showed prolonged QT interval in thalassaemia major patients compared to healthy controls.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Henriksen, Lise Fischer","Petri, Anne-Sofie","Hasselbalch, Hans Carl","Kanters, Jørgen K.","Ellervik, Christina"],"cuid":["S02-088.24-785043"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Case Control Studies","Female","Humans","Inflammation","Iron analysis","Long QT Syndrome epidemiology","Male","Middle Aged","Netherlands epidemiology","Sex Factors","Transferrin analysis","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"increased iron stores prolong the qt interval a general population study including 000000000020 000000000261 individuals and meta analysis of thalassaemia major","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84987741155","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-088.24-785043","identifier":[{"id":"27062493","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84987741155","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-2ed65669-5b34-43d1-8d08-1766fbc3c6d4","ku-12094216-ebc0-4a12-8c04-5ff7798765b6"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Case-Control Studies","Female","Ferritins/analysis","Hemochromatosis/genetics","Humans","Inflammation","Iron Overload/complications","Iron/analysis","Long QT Syndrome/epidemiology","Male","Middle Aged","Netherlands/epidemiology","Sex Factors","Transferrin/analysis","Young Adult","beta-Thalassemia/complications"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AAFFB175ADB26137F3C042E5F4F8AFEC"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Børn og Unge, R