,"first":"Matthias","key":"schleuningmatthiaspau","last":"Schleuning","name":"Schleuning, Matthias","rank":27,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Axel","key":"ssymankaxelpau","last":"Ssymank","name":"Ssymank, Axel","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Victor","key":"kakengivictorpau","last":"Kakengi","name":"Kakengi, Victor","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jie","key":"zhangjiepau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Jie","rank":30,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Katrin","key":"böhninggaesekatrinpau","last":"Böhning-Gaese","name":"Böhning-Gaese, Katrin","rank":31,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Roland","key":"brandlrolandpau","last":"Brandl","name":"Brandl, Roland","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Elisabeth K. V.","key":"kalkoelisabethkvpau","last":"Kalko","name":"Kalko, Elisabeth K. V.","rank":33,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"kleyermichaelpau","last":"Kleyer","name":"Kleyer, Michael","rank":34,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"naussthomaspau","last":"Nauss","name":"Nauss, Thomas","rank":35,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marco","key":"tschapkamarcopau","last":"Tschapka","name":"Tschapka, Marco","rank":36,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Markus","key":"fischermarkuspau","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, Markus","rank":37,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ingolf","key":"steffandewenteringolfpau","last":"Steffan-Dewenter","name":"Steffan-Dewenter, Ingolf","rank":38,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28004657"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ncomms13736","issn":["20411723"],"journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"13736","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85006874563"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-342dec06-5968-4bcb-89cf-3d03797ce05d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Predictors of elevational biodiversity gradients change from single taxa to the multi-taxa community level","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-424454","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Inflammatory reactions are involved in a diversity of diseases, including major depressive disorder. Cytokines act as intercellular signaling molecules and mediators of inflammation between the periphery and the brain. Within the brain, evidence from animal studies of acute inflammation has shown that elevated cytokine levels are linked to behavioral responses of sickness and depression-like behavior. Although chronic inflammation is more translational to human depression than acute studies, little is known on central cytokine expression and associated behavioral responses following chronic immune challenges. The present study assessed behavioral changes and a selection of cytokines in the brain and in the blood in rats randomized to receive a single or 8week administration with either lipopolysaccharide (LPS, 600μg/kg, i.p.) or saline. Acute and long-term LPS treatments caused similar sickness and depression-like behavior. Chronic LPS administration did not have an effect on blood cytokine levels, indicating endotoxin tolerance, whereas increased fasting blood glucose was observed, indicating insulin resistance, a metabolic consequence of chronic inflammation. While a single LPS injection produced a generalized cytokine response in the brain, long-term LPS administration produced a specific central cytokine response with increased interleukin (IL)-1β and interferon (IFN)-γ. These cytokines can explain the behavioral changes observed, and could indicate microglia activation, although future studies are needed to uncover this assumption. Taken together, although the behavioral outcome was similar between acute and chronic LPS administration, the central cytokine response was distinct. As the long-term LPS paradigm also posed a metabolic demand, this setting may reflect a more translational insight into inflammatory reactions in human depression, and could prove useful for assessing cytokine down-stream effects and experimental antidepressant drug products.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fischer, Christina","Elfving, Betina","Lund, Sten","Wegener, Gregers"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-154795"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"behavioral and systemic consequences of long term inflammatory challenge","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84945553970","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-154795","identifier":[{"id":"84945553970","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26531693","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-2c8289b6-148e-4cb7-b608-27a2b483049d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7560BE9717BE6341A85AD62621908131"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Translational Neuropsychiatry Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina W","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"496db6a4-7d7a-4c14-b208-10da62c375d5","name":"Fischer, Christina","name_org":"Fischer, Christina W","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Betina","key":"elfvingpau","last":"Elfving","locid":"b7b26927-4ed5-45ec-a82b-c8a860d592ca","name":"Elfving, Betina","orcid":"0000-0001-6939-5088","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sten","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"49989a7d-ae4c-4c31-8e9b-150812a78bf4","name":"Lund, Sten","orcid":"0000-0002-3805-6267","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregers","key":"wegenerpau","last":"Wegener","locid":"551a1efa-c8f3-4bb5-9931-5158061ed40a","name":"Wegener, Gregers","orcid":"0000-0002-0081-0068","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26531693"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jneuroim.2015.08.011","issn":["01655728","01695088"],"issn_org":["01655728"],"journal":"Journal of Neuroimmunology","pages":"40-6","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Neuroimmunology","volume":"288"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84945553970"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2c8289b6-148e-4cb7-b608-27a2b483049d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Behavioral and systemic consequences of long-term inflammatory challenge","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-154795","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The complex bidirectional communication between the central nervous system and the peripheral immune system is of possible relevance for both normal brain functions and the development of psychiatric disorders. The aim of this investigation was to study central expression of inflammatory markers in a genetic rat model of depression (the Flinders Sensitive line (FSL) and its control, the Flinders Resistant line (FRL)). A peripheral immune activation was induced by lipopolysaccharide (LPS) in order to investigate possible differences in immune reactions between the two rat lines. To confirm behavioural differences between the rat lines the forced swim test was performed, a test to assess depressive-like behaviour. Expression of candidate inflammatory genes was measured in amygdala, hippocampus, hypothalamus, prefrontal cortex and striatum using quantitative real time PCR. Our results show, for the first time, significantly lower central expression of the glial-specific protein S100B and complement factor C3 in several brain regions of the FSL rats compared to controls, both at baseline and after peripheral immune stimulation. No significant differences in immune responses to LPS were observed between the rats lines. Both S100B and C3 have been suggested to be of relevance for brain development and plasticity as well as brain disorders. These proteins may be of importance for the behavioural differences between the FSL and FRL rats, and this model may be useful in studies exploring the influence of the immune system on brain functions.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Strenn, Nina","Suchankova, Petra","Nilsson, Staffan","Fischer, Christina","Wegener, Gregers","Mathé, Aleksander A","Ekman, Agneta"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-154805"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chalmers University of Technology","Karolinska Institutet","University of Gothenburg"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"expression of inflammatory markers in a genetic rodent model of depression","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbr.2014.09.025","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-154805","identifier":[{"id":"25277840","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84920915040","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-2c885c54-b541-440b-a006-99d2a7b335a6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-899A22F20B380317D22FA491706956A4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbr.2014.09.025","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"university of gothenburg","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Gothenburg","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"chalmers university of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Chalmers University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University (AU)","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Translational Neuropsychiatry Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"karolinska institutet","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karolinska Institutet","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nina","key":"strennpau","last":"Strenn","name":"Strenn, Nina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Petra","key":"suchankovapau","last":"Suchankova","name":"Suchankova, Petra","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Staffan","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","name":"Nilsson, Staffan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"496db6a4-7d7a-4c14-b208-10da62c375d5","name":"Fischer, Christina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregers","key":"wegenerpau","last":"Wegener","locid":"551a1efa-c8f3-4bb5-9931-5158061ed40a","name":"Wegener, Gregers","orcid":"0000-0002-0081-0068","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleksander A","key":"mathépau","last":"Mathé","name":"Mathé, Aleksander A","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Agneta","key":"ekmanpau","last":"Ekman","name":"Ekman, Agneta","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25277840"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.bbr.2014.09.025","issn":["01664328","18727549"],"issn_org":["01664328"],"journal":"Behavioural Brain Research","pages":"348-357","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Behavioural Brain Research","volume":"281"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84920915040"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2c885c54-b541-440b-a006-99d2a7b335a6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Expression of inflammatory markers in a genetic rodent model of depression","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-154805","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
