{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Fischer, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-233207"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"challenging the immune system in rodents and its association to depression","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dtd","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-233207","ids":["au-b612e8ba-8ebc-4fb1-8a27-35e72968175e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E38696B216A73F2142081857F0A03A5B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Translational Neuropsychiatry Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"496db6a4-7d7a-4c14-b208-10da62c375d5","name":"Fischer, Christina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"176","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b612e8ba-8ebc-4fb1-8a27-35e72968175e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Challenging the immune system in rodents and its association to depression","type":"Thesis Doctoral","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-233207","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Obesity-related inflammation may have a causal role in the development of diabetes and insulin resistance, and studies using animal models of chronic experimental endotoxemia have shown the link. However, many studies use only males, and much less is known about the role of obesity-related inflammation in females. Therefore, we addressed how experimentally induced chronic inflammation affects body mass, energy intake, and glucose metabolism in female rats. Adult female Sprague Dawley rats were instrumented with slow release pellets that delivered a constant daily dose of 53 or 207 μg of lipopolysaccharide (LPS) per rat for 60 days. Control rats were instrumented with vehicle pellets. Due to inflammatory nature of high-fat diet (HFD) half of the rats received HFD (60% of calories from lard), while the other half remained on control diet to detect possible interactions between two modes of induced inflammation. Our results showed that chronic LPS administration increased female rat body mass and calorie intake in a dose-dependent manner, and that HFD further exacerbated these effects. Despite these effects, no effects of LPS and HFD were evident on female rat glucose metabolism. Only LPS elevated expression of inflammatory markers in the hypothalamus. To conclude, female rats respond to experimentally induced chronic inflammation by increasing body mass, but do not develop glucose intolerance in the given period of time.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Dudele, Anete","Fischer, Christina","Elfving, Betina","Wegener, Gregers","Wang, Tobias","Lund, Sten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-235487"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chronic exposure to low doses of lipopolysaccharide and high fat feeding increases body mass without affecting glucose tolerance in female rats","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84977618026","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-235487","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4673625","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"26537342","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84977618026","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b9f818d8-0c44-458d-a4e1-df0c229468c7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9E40E762E9F3074988FF7A366EF942A2"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Zoophysiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anete","key":"dudelepau","last":"Dudele","locid":"1b249b21-b57e-469e-823d-8feddabfdb2a","name":"Dudele, Anete","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina W","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"496db6a4-7d7a-4c14-b208-10da62c375d5","name":"Fischer, Christina","name_org":"Fischer, Christina W","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Betina","key":"elfvingpau","last":"Elfving","locid":"b7b26927-4ed5-45ec-a82b-c8a860d592ca","name":"Elfving, Betina","orcid":"0000-0001-6939-5088","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregers","key":"wegenerpau","last":"Wegener","locid":"551a1efa-c8f3-4bb5-9931-5158061ed40a","name":"Wegener, Gregers","orcid":"0000-0002-0081-0068","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"7a3d91ab-5dbf-46e4-bc6e-634e16bd8d80","name":"Wang, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0002-4350-3682","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sten","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"49989a7d-ae4c-4c31-8e9b-150812a78bf4","name":"Lund, Sten","orcid":"0000-0002-3805-6267","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26537342"],"pub":{"doi":"10.14814/phy2.12584","issn":["2051817X"],"issue":"11","journal":"Physiological Reports","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Physiological Reports","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84977618026"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b9f818d8-0c44-458d-a4e1-df0c229468c7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Chronic exposure to low doses of lipopolysaccharide and high-fat feeding increases body mass without affecting glucose tolerance in female rats","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-235487","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Immunotherapy with the cytokine interferon-alpha (IFN-α) can induce symptoms of depression, and it is likely that the tryptophan-kynurenine pathway may be involved in this regard. In this study we investigated the effects of IFN-α on depression-like behaviour and central metabolites of the tryptophan-kynurenine pathway in rats. Secondly, we explored the modulating effects of an antidepressant (imipramine) and anti-inflammatory drug (celecoxib) on IFN-α-induced behavioural and pathophysiological changes in the brain. The following treatment groups were used: Control (saline), IFN-α (6×10(4) IU/kg s.c.), IFN-α + imipramine or IFN-α + celecoxib. Drugs were administered daily for 1 week. IFN-α treatment induced depression-like behaviour by increasing immobility in the forced swim test (FST), and decreased tryptophan levels in the brain. There was a trend for an increased kynurenine/tryptophan ratio, indicative of indoleamine 2,3-dioxygenase (IDO) activation, and increased quinolinic acid in the hippocampus. Imipramine decreased immobility in the FST, but did not reverse the IFN-α-induced changes in the tryptophan-kynurenine pathway. There was a trend for celecoxib to decrease immobility and to reverse the IFN-α-induced increase in the kynurenine/tryptophan ratio. Thus, our study provides further evidence for IFN-α-induced depression-like behaviour through central changes of the tryptophan-kynurenine pathway.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Fischer, Christina","Eskelund, Amanda","Budac, David P","Tillmann, Sandra","Liebenberg, Nico","Elfving, Betina","Wegener, Gregers"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-179806"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"interferon alpha treatment induces depression like behaviour accompanied by elevated hippocampal quinolinic acid levels in rats","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbr.2015.07.015","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-179806","identifier":[{"id":"84938080484","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26205824","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-5880b66c-ea2d-49be-8111-78316b9d912e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DC546F2F95A282567B605A6E667CD2E9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbr.2015.07.015","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Translational Neuropsychiatry Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Weide","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"496db6a4-7d7a-4c14-b208-10da62c375d5","name":"Fischer, Christina","name_org":"Fischer, Christina Weide","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amanda","key":"eskelundpau","last":"Eskelund","locid":"b3efadf2-1392-4776-a7ac-3d50978d9be5","name":"Eskelund, Amanda","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"David P","key":"budacpau","last":"Budac","name":"Budac, David P","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sandra","key":"tillmannpau","last":"Tillmann","locid":"f53bbfac-c060-49c3-9e34-44e45462df79","name":"Tillmann, Sandra","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nico","key":"liebenbergpau","last":"Liebenberg","locid":"88420522-5e97-422f-a396-e7f6b0370515","name":"Liebenberg, Nico","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Betina","key":"elfvingpau","last":"Elfving","locid":"b7b26927-4ed5-45ec-a82b-c8a860d592ca","name":"Elfving, Betina","orcid":"0000-0001-6939-5088","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregers","key":"wegenerpau","last":"Wegener","locid":"551a1efa-c8f3-4bb5-9931-5158061ed40a","name":"Wegener, Gregers","orcid":"0000-0002-0081-0068","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26205824"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.bbr.2015.07.015","issn":["01664328","18727549"],"issn_org":["01664328"],"journal":"Behavioural Brain Research","pages":"166-172","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Behavioural Brain Research","volume":"293"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84938080484"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5880b66c-ea2d-49be-8111-78316b9d912e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Interferon-alpha treatment induces depression-like behaviour accompanied by elevated hippocampal quinolinic acid levels in rats","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-179806","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Regular endurance exercise promotes metabolic and oxidative changes in skeletal muscle. Overexpression of interleukin-15 (IL-15) in mice exerts similar metabolic changes in muscle as seen with endurance exercise. Muscular IL-15 production has been shown to increase in mice after weeks of regular endurance running. With the present study we aimed to determine if muscular IL-15 production would increase in human male subjects following 12 weeks of endurance training. In two different studies we obtained plasma and muscle biopsies from young healthy subjects performing: (1) 12 weeks of ergometer cycling exercise five times per week with plasma and biopsies before and after the intervention, and (2) 3 h of ergometer cycling exercise with plasma and biopsies before and after the exercise bout and well into recovery. We measured changes in plasma IL-15, muscle IL-15 mRNA and IL-15 protein. Twelve weeks of regular endurance training induced a 40% increase in basal skeletal muscle IL-15 protein content (p","author_count":8,"contributors":["Rinnov, Anders","Yfanti, Christina","Nielsen, Søren","Åkerström, Thorbjörn","Peijs, Lone","Zankari, Alaa","Fischer, Christian Philip","Pedersen, Bente Klarlund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-422545"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"endurance training enhances skeletal muscle interleukin 000000000015 in human male subjects","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12020-013-9969-z","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-422545","identifier":[{"id":"23649460","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84896717042","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-30d8e535-8cd2-4502-9a24-5d3d9be619c7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5A136A61A952282B23B2123C5916E9D7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12020-013-9969-z","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, The August Krogh Section for Human Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"rinnovpau","last":"Rinnov","name":"Rinnov, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"yfantipau","last":"Yfanti","name":"Yfanti, Christina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Søren","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thorbjörn","key":"åkerströmpau","last":"Åkerström","locid":"44559d6f-7705-41e4-8c22-5fb0fe1c9b6d","name":"Åkerström, Thorbjörn","orcid":"0000-0002-7330-1723","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lone","key":"peijspau","last":"Peijs","name":"Peijs, Lone","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Alaa","key":"zankaripau","last":"Zankari","name":"Zankari, Alaa","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian Philip","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"a17260a4-4ec1-41e8-85be-97659b87b98d","name":"Fischer, Christian Philip","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Bente Klarlund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5d38d54e-e0d1-4397-98ca-6d8c9b78606d","name":"Pedersen, Bente Klarlund","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23649460"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s12020-013-9969-z","issn":["1355008X","15590100"],"issn_org":["1355008X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Endocrine","pages":"271-278","status":"p","title":"Endocrine","volume":"45"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84896717042"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-30d8e535-8cd2-4502-9a24-5d3d9be619c7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Endurance training enhances skeletal muscle interleukin-15 in human male subjects","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-422545","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Burnout is characterized by emotional exhaustion, depersonalization and reduced personal accomplishment. In agreement with international studies, Danish figures have revealed an increase in prevalence of severe burnout from 2.8% in 2004 to 5.3% in 2012. There is only little research on the consequences for the burned-out general practitioner (GP) and his patients as well as on appropriate intervention strategies. Even though burnout appears to be caused by a combination of personality factors and environmental conditions, the literature has one-sidedly focused on the resilience of the individual GP.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Pedersen, Anette Fischer","Andersen, Christina Maar","Olesen, Frede","Vedsted, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-255261"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"stress og udbrændthed hos alment praktiserende læger er stigende","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84893449937","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-255261","identifier":[{"id":"24629678","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84893449937","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-dca4a85e-b14e-4a8b-a268-eb6cf7cdd43e"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-0DDCBEDEC3C67E9B9ECE76A6F5EB4AA5"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Departm